          <Pad Id="kFx8B1p0xKOfsm3oWSLeX9" Bounds="85,745,830,127" ShowValueBox="true" isIOBox="true" Value="Notes:&#xD;&#xA;- Tearing: the display shows parts of two frames at once, so the edges of fast horizontal motion break into a step. The bars (one LFO through SineWave and Map to the window width, 10 units here) make it easy to see.&#xD;&#xA;- To compare, set VSync to false and look at the diagonal edges while the bars move; set it back to true and they stay clean. The pin is read when the window is created, so each change recreates the window.&#xD;&#xA;- VSync true waits for the display refresh inside Present. With several VSync windows the waits add up in one pump, so each window runs at about refresh / number of windows; the vvvv main loop is blocked with them. Tracked in VL.Qt issue 90.&#xD;&#xA;- The window size is set on the Renderer (Bounds, 1000 x 500 DIP = 10 x 5 units); the Map range matches it.">
            <p:TypeAnnotation LastCategoryFullName="Primitive" LastDependency="CoreLibBasics.vl">
              <Choice Kind="TypeFlag" Name="String" />
            </p:TypeAnnotation>
            <p:ValueBoxSettings>
              <p:fontsize p:Type="Int32">9</p:fontsize>
              <p:stringtype p:Assembly="VL.Core" p:Type="VL.Core.StringType">Comment</p:stringtype>
            </p:ValueBoxSettings>
          </Pad>
